Actually, let me reconsider. Keira brings $300 upfront and 60 items — the most — which could mean strong sales. Even at 25%, if she sells well, both parties benefit. But Dev's lower 10% share means I keep more per sale, and $260 upfront is still strong. 

I'll go with Dev — best balance of upfront, low share, good quantity, and easy setup time.

